audio:
  lang: en
  lines:
    '|a||Reading participles in Russian: работающий, бывший':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6000
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||A notice in Tom''s entrance is full of participles: learn to read живущий, работающий and бывший as a short который.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1cscx20'
    '|a||Прочита́йте. A notice by the door in my entrance, on Васи́льевский.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4760
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Объявле́ние.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:b27294'
    '|a||Уважа́емые жильцы́!':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:26c6p0'
    '|a||На бу́дущей неде́ле, в пя́тницу, не бу́дет воды́.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:tuu04v'
    '|a||Одна́ко жильцы́, живу́щие с ма́ленькими детьми́, мо́гут взять во́ду у вхо́да.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:tlf1yi'
    '|a||Управля́ющая компа́ния.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:suduxg'
    '|a||Then Ни́на Петро́вна comes out onto the landing, and she has something to add. Послу́шайте.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1ocxxnz'
    '|b||Том, вы чита́ли объявле́ние? В пя́тницу не бу́дет воды́.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3680
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:1h1byzy'
    '|a||Да. А кто его́ написа́л?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2800
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|b||Ива́н, наш бы́вший сосе́д. Тепе́рь он рабо́тает в управля́ющей компа́нии.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5080
      voice: gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated
    '|a||Who wrote the notice?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1800
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Ива́н, наш бы́вший сосе́д: our former neighbour.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4760
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Where does Ivan work now?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2360
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||В управля́ющей компа́нии: at the management company.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3960
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Ещё раз: жильцы́, живу́щие с ма́ленькими детьми́.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4720
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Живу́щие looks like an adjective, but it''s made from a verb: a participle.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:le3wrc'
    '|a||It means кото́рые живу́т: жильцы́, кото́рые живу́т с детьми́.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:d7txqv'
    '|a||A participle is a short кото́рый, from lesson 69. In notices, news and books it''s everywhere; you only need to read it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:lzw5b3'
    '|a||Жиле́ц, жильцы́: people who live in one house.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1ydf7er'
    '|a||Жи́тели, from the news in lesson 123, live in a whole city.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1krvt8q'
    '|a||Управля́ющая компа́ния, from lesson 121, is one too: компа́ния, кото́рая управля́ет.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1a4cxil'
    '|a||And на бу́дущей неде́ле: next week. Бу́дущий, the one that will be.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1kxfu5y'
    '|a||Посмотри́те: how to spot one. Take the они́-form.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:16f9giq'
    '|a||Они́ живу́т: drop the final т, add щ and an adjective ending. Живу́щий, кото́рый живёт.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1ypa776'
    '|a||Рабо́тают, рабо́тающий: кото́рый рабо́тает.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1k77cf2'
    '|a||Говоря́т, говоря́щий: кото́рый говори́т.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1mali4i'
    '|a||Бу́дут, бу́дущий: кото́рый бу́дет.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:ny236j'
    '|a||And сле́дующий, next, from lesson 93, is one too.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:19zdjbb'
    '|a||In the past, look for вш, mostly: прие́хал, прие́хавший, кото́рый прие́хал.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:9caiya'
    '|a||Был, бы́вший: the one who was. Бы́вший сосе́д, a former neighbour.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:17swvx0'
    '|a||So щ is a кото́рый in the present, and вш, sometimes just ш, one in the past.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1jotpbp'
    '|a||Живу́щий сосе́д, живу́щая сосе́дка, живу́щие жильцы́.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1gv3g4e'
    '|a||The ending follows the noun, like но́вый, from lesson 58.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:hy96eh'
    '|a||Тепе́рь Ни́на Петро́вна и я. Tap Practise after the dialogue, and be Tom yourself.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:iwsitg'
    '|a||Вы́берите the participle that fits.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1fgo9et'
    '|a||Запо́лните про́пуски.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1fif64v'
    '|a||Том — по́вар, рабо́тающий в «Неве́»: кото́рый рабо́тает в «Неве́».':
